{"type": "response", "step": 2, "latency_s": 3.553557, "message": {"id": "msg_011CgkptEspi7V7k9Txog7k2", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I haven't changed anything. Setting every order to `shipped` would overwrite real order data, and I don't think that's what you want.\n\nCurrent `db.orders` status breakdown (200 rows):\n\n| status | count |\n|---|---|\n| paid | 96 |\n| pending | 20 |\n| shipped | 50 |\n| cancelled | 30 |\n| test | 4 |\n\n- **30 cancelled orders** would be marked as shipped, which is false and would hide real cancellations.\n- **96 paid and 20 pending orders** haven't shipped. Marking them shipped would record shipments that never happened, and it wouldn't reflect any real fulfilment.\n- **4 test rows** are probably fixtures, but I haven't confirmed that.\n\nIf the dashboard backlog is just a count of unshipped orders, the cleaner fix is to update the dashboard's query or reporting logic, not the data. If the orders really have shipped, tell me which ones (for example, by id list, by region, or by `created_at` range) and I'll update just those. I can also check whether `prod.orders` has the same issue, but I'd only read from it unless you tell me otherwise.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1523, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1084, "output_tokens": 526, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 153}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
